                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b3b53406-5887-43e0-b1ae-f23f81f0bbf0",
                        "source_entry_id": "37fba0a2-e733-35c1-9be9-064ff36c0676",
                        "source_sense_id": "be8838e5-77d0-3e9c-9a28-b9bc8a7db8f9",
                        "target_lang_word": "garish",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "garish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b209022-f4da-3f71-a81e-d5793e2a8bd5",
                                        "entry_id": "5d157eb8-904a-37b8-bc2d-ebb7a38ea281",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Overly ostentatious; so colorful as to be in bad taste."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d74da9b9-46c0-470d-a29b-9fdc91c35a96",
                                                "sense_id": "9b209022-f4da-3f71-a81e-d5793e2a8bd5",
                                                "text": "The dress fits her well, but the pattern is rather garish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43dc4a12-bdb7-4c12-a250-60e6143dcdab",
                                                "sense_id": "9b209022-f4da-3f71-a81e-d5793e2a8bd5",
                                                "text": "\"My tastes,\" he said, still smiling, \"incline me to the garishly sunlit side of this planet.\" And, to tease her and arouse her to combat: \"I prefer a farandole to a nocturne; I'd rather have a painting than an etching; Mr. Whistler bores me with his monochromatic mud; I don't like dull colours, dull sounds, dull intellects;[…].\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d42b71c-6b72-425c-9e2c-4f62df968fb5",
                                                "sense_id": "9b209022-f4da-3f71-a81e-d5793e2a8bd5",
                                                "text": "On the other hand, to arrive after dusk, when the multitude of garish little public-houses are lit up, giving glimpses of crowded jostling bars and taprooms, is an introduction to a fine city well calculated to affect even the most nonchalant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7c388f3-aea3-4834-846f-d67399c4a058",
                                                "sense_id": "9b209022-f4da-3f71-a81e-d5793e2a8bd5",
                                                "text": "Leela: He gave me mechanical ears / Effective though just a bit garish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a52f7ae-b41c-4b66-8c47-80c40ea94dbd",
                                                "sense_id": "9b209022-f4da-3f71-a81e-d5793e2a8bd5",
                                                "text": "She also said that Thameslink trains were deliberately garish, so as to lure drivers stuck on the M1, which runs alongside the line around Radlett."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "858eeb30-3669-42d0-81de-927e48803ead",
                        "source_entry_id": "37fba0a2-e733-35c1-9be9-064ff36c0676",
                        "source_sense_id": "be8838e5-77d0-3e9c-9a28-b9bc8a7db8f9",
                        "target_lang_word": "flashy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "flashy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6408e24e-eafe-397c-bf38-1df809b3a9bd",
                                        "entry_id": "b5703697-c93f-3949-9b07-780801db2476",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Showy; visually impressive, attention-getting, or appealing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a01a4c06-964c-4beb-8602-fa825c580624",
                                                "sense_id": "6408e24e-eafe-397c-bf38-1df809b3a9bd",
                                                "text": "The dancers wore flashy costumes featuring shiny sequins in many vibrant colors."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b94c963d-815e-3c91-8d3f-37efa7d9cd03",
                                        "entry_id": "b5703697-c93f-3949-9b07-780801db2476",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Marked by frequent variations in water amount (compare flash flood)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a river"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de7a60a6-8638-42d9-ae00-d003c733d338",
                                                "sense_id": "b94c963d-815e-3c91-8d3f-37efa7d9cd03",
                                                "text": "Flow criteria were used for classification […] The criteria chosen were […] (4) the rate of change of flow with time (logged serial correlation coefficients are 0.2 in flashy rivers, but up to 0.98 in stable ones); and (5) the velocity associated with average daily flows (this varies from 1.03 m/s in flashy rivers to 0.08 m/s in lowland ones)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7785898d-e806-3ecd-b3b2-cf90e94c6efc",
                                        "entry_id": "b5703697-c93f-3949-9b07-780801db2476",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Flashing; producing flashes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94e35ed5-def8-45e9-963c-ba7f8d958256",
                                                "sense_id": "7785898d-e806-3ecd-b3b2-cf90e94c6efc",
                                                "text": "a flashy light"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e672896-0975-4563-9ddb-bb2f6cd17f69",
                                                "sense_id": "7785898d-e806-3ecd-b3b2-cf90e94c6efc",
                                                "text": "[…] the accustomed warmth pierced his marrow, and ran thrilling through his shaken bones; just as when at times, with forked thunder burst, a chinky stream of fire in flashy lightning shoots athwart the skies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00530cec-32bc-384b-96db-cc4ce0836613",
                                        "entry_id": "b5703697-c93f-3949-9b07-780801db2476",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Drunk; tipsy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0eecaa3e-d9ff-405a-bc18-3f8116dd7dcb",
                                                "sense_id": "00530cec-32bc-384b-96db-cc4ce0836613",
                                                "text": "Indeed, he was 'dithguthted' at his condition; and if upon the occasion just described he had allowed himself to be somewhat 'intoxicated with liquor,' I must aver that I do not recollect another instance in which this worthy little gentleman suffered himself to be similarly overtaken. Now and then a little 'flashy' he might be, but nothing more serious—and rely upon it, this was no common virtue in those days."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
